`  | `uuid | session name`  | Resume the specified session. Omit and use `--last` to continue the most recent session.\nL2891: Key\nL2892: \nL2893: `--all`\nL2894: \nL2895: Type / Values\nL2896: \nL2897: `boolean`\nL2898: \nL2899: Details\nL2900: \nL2901: Include sessions outside the current working directory when selecting the most recent session.\nL2902: \nL2903: Key\nL2904: \nL2905: `--include-non-interactive`\nL2906: \nL2907: Type / Values\nL2908: \nL2909: `boolean`\nL2910: \nL2911: Details\nL2912: \nL2913: Include non-interactive sessions in the picker and `--last` selection.\nL2914: \nL2915: Key\nL2916: \nL2917: `--last`\nL2918: \nL2919: Type / Values\nL2920: \nL2921: `boolean`\nL2922: \nL2923: Details\nL2924: \nL2925: Skip the picker and resume the most recent chat from the current working directory.\nL2926: \nL2927: Key\nL2928: \nL2929: `SESSION_ID`\nL2930: \nL2931: Type / Values\nL2932: \nL2933: `uuid | session name`\nL2934: \nL2935: Details\nL2936: Resume the specified session. Omit and use `--last` to continue the most recent session.\nL2937: ### `codex fork`\nL2938: \nL2939: Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat. By default, `codex fork` opens the session picker; add `--last` to fork your most recent session instead.\nL2940: \nL2941: When the current and saved session directories differ, `codex fork` uses the same working-directory prompt and `tui.resume_cwd` setting as `codex resume`.\nL2942: \nL2943: [Input: Filter by key, type, or details]\nL2944: Key  | Type / Values  | Details\nL2945: --- | --- | ---\nL2946: `--all`  | `boolean`  | Show sessions beyond the current working directory in the picker.\nL2947: `--last`  | `boolean`  | Skip the picker and fork the most recent chat automatically.\nL2948: `SESSION_ID`  | `uuid`  | Fork the specified session. Omit and use `--last` to fork the most recent session.\nL2949: \nL2950: Key\nL2951: \nL2952: `--all`\nL2953: \nL2954: Type / Values\nL2955: \nL2956: `boolean`\nL2957: \nL2958: Details\nL295